{
  "name": "Job Agent 02 — Tailor & Apply",
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1",
    "saveManualExecutions": true,
    "callerPolicy": "workflowsFromSameOwner"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "sticky-overview",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -460,
        -220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 440,
        "height": 380,
        "content": "## 02 — Tailor & Apply\n\nPicks up everything left at `status = queued` and works one job at a time.\n\n**The status column is the resume mechanism.** If this workflow dies halfway, tomorrow's run picks up the remaining `queued` rows with no recovery logic.\n\n**Nothing is submitted while `DRY_RUN=true` in .env** (the default). Forms get filled and screenshotted, then abandoned. Jobs stay `queued`, so nothing is lost while you look at the screenshots in `apply-svc/artifacts/`.\n\nCaps come from .env: `MAX_APPLICATIONS_PER_RUN`, `MIN_DELAY_MS`, `MAX_DELAY_MS`.\n\nYou need **Google Sheets** and **Google Drive** under Credentials."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "trigger-apply",
      "name": "Apply Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 10 * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "notes": "An hour after workflow 01 so scoring has finished."
    },
    {
      "id": "load-profile",
      "name": "Load Profile",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "@@include:00-load-profile.js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sheet-read",
      "name": "Read Jobs Sheet",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        440,
        0
      ],
      "alwaysOutputData": true,
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "read",
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ $('Load Profile').first().json.config.sheet_id }}"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "jobs"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "select-queued",
      "name": "Select Queued Jobs",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        660,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "@@include:08-select-queued.js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "loop",
      "name": "Loop Over Jobs",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.splitInBatches",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [
        880,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "batchSize": 1,
        "options": {
          "reset": false
        }
      },
      "notes": "Concurrency 1. Bursts get throttled far harder than steady traffic."
    },
    {
      "id": "route-ats",
      "name": "Route ATS",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1120,
        120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "@@include:09-route-ats.js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "req-tailor",
      "name": "Build Tailor Request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1340,
        120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "@@include:req-tailor.js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "claude-tailor",
      "name": "AI: Tailor Resume",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1560,
        120
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 2,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000,
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $json._llm.url }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json._llm.body) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 300000
        },
        "specifyHeaders": "json",
        "jsonHeaders": "={{ JSON.stringify($json._llm.headers) }}"
      },
      "notes": "Endpoint, auth header and body all come from $json._llm, which lib.js builds for whichever LLM_PROVIDER is set in .env. Nothing here is provider-specific, so switching AI never touches this node."
    },
    {
      "id": "render-html",
      "name": "Render Resume HTML",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1780,
        120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "@@include:10-render-resume-html.js"
      },
      "notes": "Single column, real headings, no tables or icons. Two-column templates are the most common reason a good resume scores badly in ATS parsers."
    },
    {
      "id": "req-cover",
      "name": "Build Cover Letter Request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        2000,
        120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "@@include:req-cover.js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "claude-cover",
      "name": "AI: Cover Letter",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        2220,
        120
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 2,
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $json._llm.url }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json._llm.body) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 120000
        },
        "specifyHeaders": "json",
        "jsonHeaders": "={{ JSON.stringify($json._llm.headers) }}"
      },
      "notes": "Endpoint, auth header and body all come from $json._llm, which lib.js builds for whichever LLM_PROVIDER is set in .env. Nothing here is provider-specific, so switching AI never touches this node."
    },
    {
      "id": "merge-cover",
      "name": "Merge Cover Letter",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        2440,
        120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "@@include:13-merge-cover.js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "render-pdf",
      "name": "Render PDF",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        2660,
        120
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 2,
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $('Load Profile').first().json.config.apply_svc_url }}/render-pdf",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "x-apply-token",
              "value": "={{ $('Load Profile').first().json.config.apply_token }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "content-type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ html: $json.resume_html, filename: $json.resume_filename }) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 60000,
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "responseFormat": "file",
              "outputPropertyName": "data"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": "apply-svc already runs Playwright, so page.pdf() replaces an entire external PDF service."
    },
    {
      "id": "drive-resume",
      "name": "Upload Resume to Drive",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleDrive",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [
        2880,
        120
      ],
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "upload",
        "inputDataFieldName": "data",
        "name": "={{ $('Merge Cover Letter').item.json.resume_filename }}",
        "driveId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "My Drive"
        },
        "folderId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "root"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "notes": "Keeps the exact PDF that was submitted. When a recruiter replies in three weeks you will want to know which version they read."
    },
    {
      "id": "req-apply",
      "name": "Build Apply Request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        3100,
        120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "@@include:11-build-apply-request.js"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "submit",
      "name": "Submit Application",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        3320,
        120
      ],
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $json._apply_url }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "x-apply-token",
              "value": "={{ $('Load Profile').first().json.config.apply_token }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "content-type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json._body) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 300000
        }
      },
      "notes": "Long timeout: a paced submission includes a 45-120s human-like delay."
    },
    {
      "id": "record",
      "name": "Record Outcome",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        3540,
        120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "@@include:12-record-outcome.js"
      }
